    ("The weekly Sabbath stands outside Romans 14 and Colossians 2", "Lee; Baidoo in part", "“Every day alike” is approved; “sabbath days” is in the list; the sign was Israel’s", "17.2; chapters 3, 12"),
    ("“Do all to the glory of God” is the one rule", "Constable", "Paul gives particulars before the sentence, on other grounds", "17.3; chapter 9"),
    ("“Destroy” and “perish” mean lost salvation", "Some commentaries; Piper on the stakes", "Paul does not define them; the weight is “for whom Christ died”", "17.4; chapters 4, 6"),
    ("Romans 14:23 is a general rule of doubt", "Some commentaries", "The “for” joins it to the man who eats", "17.5; chapter 4"),
    ("Colossians 2 and Romans 14 conflict", "Some commentaries", "They draw one boundary from two sides", "17.6; chapter 12"),
